body:
MOVIE-LEAD DISPOSITION — ACCEPT standoff, D3 accounting, report/interchange separation, and multiple declared coordinate views. Add a future movie-profile contract; do not broaden the initial ASCII CLI slice by accident.

I adopt the owner boundary exactly as corrected: obvious preview.html; direct filesystem opening by ordinary browser action; no build step, terminal, local server, or installation. I do not treat no-JavaScript, one-file, offline, no-network, or bundle-local assets as owner law. My engineering preference for a reproducible offline profile is a proposal only.

For movies, source.txt cannot be generalized into a fake universal source artifact. The future bundle needs a checked media/source manifest that binds bundle, edition, rendition, streams, checksums, axes, occurrences, and admitted access disposition. Movie bytes may be Included, ExternalAdmitted, or Unavailable; size and rights often prevent embedding them. The report must remain scientifically inspectable when playback bytes are absent, and an unavailable player must render as an explicit availability state rather than blank media. Derived frames/audio remain evidence-bearing artifacts with their own rights and receipts, not replacements for the source.

The visualization must keep five coordinate roles distinct: edition playback axis, native stream coordinates, story-world time, recall time, and optional scanner/behaviour time. JavaScript may synchronize selection, seek through an admitted checked mapping, filter tracks, and switch declared projections. It may not equate numeric timestamps, infer chronology from layout, bridge a mapping gap, select the first reverse preimage, or manufacture a causal/identity relation in the browser. One preview document is fine; one scientific geometry is not. Codex remains the discourse/evidence reading; playback, chronology/causality/hierarchy, and recall-alignment views are sibling declared projections linked by stable addresses.

D3 is especially load-bearing for film. No picture sample while audio continues is not an empty event. No thumbnail can mean not sampled, unavailable media, outside the view horizon, failed extraction, ineligible, or explicit absence; those must not share rendered silence. Likewise subtitle not present, subtitle track not admitted, ASR failed, and speech absent are different states. Measured zero remains measured. Every requested eligible address must be represented by a mark or an explicit render disposition.

Movie-profile acceptance courts:
1. an audio-only edition interval remains seekable/accounted while picture has no sample;
2. repeated or flashback material retains occurrence identity and all reverse preimages;
3. equal numeric timestamps in alternate editions never cross-highlight without correspondence;
4. a mapping gap cannot be visually bridged by an edge or playback cursor;
5. ExternalAdmitted media missing at open yields an explicit availability panel while narrative/evidence inventories remain usable;
6. source paths with spaces/non-ASCII open under the owner local profile;
7. measured, absent, imputed, ineligible, unresolved/failed, excluded, filtered, and off-projection states remain locally distinguishable without colour alone and in the textual twin.

A future movie bundle can extend the proposed source/storymodel/result/preview/manifest roles with media-manifest and optional manifest-bound evidence assets. The initial text success bundle should stay narrow. This is a format disposition under the landed movie architecture, not implementation or media-admission authority.
